# Read by: the XDG autostart mechanism — under systemd, systemd-xdg-autostart-generator,
# which niri pulls in through xdg-desktop-autostart.target.
#
# REPLACES the file of the same name shipped by the xwaylandvideobridge package. The only
# change from upstream is the NotShowIn line at the bottom; everything above it is
# upstream's entry, so the bridge behaves exactly as before in a Plasma session.
#
# WHY: the Xwayland Video Bridge republishes a Wayland screen capture as an X11 window so
# X11 applications (Discord, Zoom, older OBS) can record the screen. It is meant to be
# invisible and leaves that to the compositor — KDE ships a KWin rule, niri has none. A
# window rule in /etc/niri/config.kdl keeps the window from being drawn (DD-019), but a
# hidden window is still a window: it stays in niri's toplevel list and so keeps showing up
# in DankMaterialShell's bar, and neither niri nor DMS can filter it out. The only way to
# get it out of the bar is not to start it.
#
# COST: X11 applications cannot capture the screen in the Niri session. Wayland-native
# screen sharing, through xdg-desktop-portal, is unaffected. Run `xwaylandvideobridge` by
# hand when an X11 application needs it.
#
# The localized Name/Comment/GenericName entries upstream carries are omitted: NoDisplay
# is true, so this entry is never shown to a user and they have nothing to translate.
#
# See docs/desktops.md and docs/design-decisions.md DD-019, DD-021.

[Desktop Entry]
StartupNotify=false
X-KDE-autostart-phase=2
X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true
NoDisplay=true

Type=Application
Name=Xwayland Video Bridge
GenericName=Share screens and windows to XWayland applications
Icon=org.kde.xwaylandvideobridge
Exec=xwaylandvideobridge
Categories=Qt;KDE;Utility;X-KDE-Utilities-Desktop;

# Everything above this line is upstream's entry, verbatim.
# niri sets XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=niri, which is what this matches. Lower-case, as niri
# spells it; the match is case-sensitive.
NotShowIn=niri;
